cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Certified worst-case intervals with a matched permutation null for
  spatial co-expression contrasts under molecule reassignment
message: >-
  If you use this code or the certified-interval construction, please cite the
  accompanying manuscript and this repository.
authors:
  - given-names: Amy
    family-names: Wang
version: 1.0.3
date-released: "2026-10-22"
repository-code: "https://github.com/amywang2010/lr-certificates"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Per-contrast intervals for a co-expression score in spatial transcriptomics,
  valid over a declared set of molecule-to-cell reassignments (boundary-local
  reassignment with per-cell capacity constraints, mask erosion and dilation,
  and a parameterised donor radius). The reported interval is a sound superset
  of the attainable range. Certification has two layers: the interval sign, and
  a claim status that additionally requires a permutation null which recomputes
  the same worst-case object under every label permutation, with within-region
  false-discovery control. The sign refers to a declared reference level of the
  score, not to a biological direction. Evaluated on three public Xenium
  sections spanning two tissues, two panel densities and two tumour types.
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - molecule reassignment
  - robust bounds
  - matched permutation null
  - co-expression
  - uncertainty quantification
